<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Alexandria on Gardens of the Roman Empire</title><link>https://roman-gardens.github.io/test-drafts/id/6ad907e90b/</link><description>Recent content in Alexandria on Gardens of the Roman Empire</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Tue, 14 Jul 2026 15:53:37 -0400</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://roman-gardens.github.io/test-drafts/id/6ad907e90b/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Garden at Kanopos</title><link>https://roman-gardens.github.io/test-drafts/id/05b24acec3/</link><pubDate>Thu, 07 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://roman-gardens.github.io/test-drafts/id/05b24acec3/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="dates"&gt;Dates&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;22 BCE&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="excavation-dates"&gt;Excavation Dates&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;unexcavated&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="garden-description"&gt;Garden Description&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This garden was in wetlands (&lt;em&gt;tenagos&lt;/em&gt;) by the Strip (&lt;em&gt;tainias&lt;/em&gt;, a ridge) (cf. Fraser 1972: II, 253-54 n. 96). Size lost. Leased in 22 BCE for one year, rent part in cash and part in produce. Crops mentioned in the &lt;a href="https://papyri.info/hgv/18560" target="_blank"&gt;preserved text&lt;/a&gt; are: garden lettuce (&lt;em&gt;θρίδακας κηπουριακὰς&lt;/em&gt;); wild lettuce; fresh grapes; gourds; plantains; beetroot; leeks (headed and sweet); a member of the cabbage family (probably cauliflower); and land snails.&lt;/p&gt;
